------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party dependencies
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

OpenReagent depends, at runtime, on the following libraries. Each is the
property of its respective authors and is distributed under its own license.
These libraries are not redistributed as part of this source tree; they are
declared as dependencies and installed separately.

Core (always required):
  - pydantic            MIT License
  - typer               MIT License
  - rich                MIT License

Optional extras (installed only when the corresponding feature is used):
  - py-solc-x           MIT License        (extra: bytecode)
  - eth-hash            MIT License        (extra: bytecode)
  - pyevmasm            Apache-2.0 License (extra: bytecode)
  - datasketch          MIT License        (extra: sketch)
  - pg8000              BSD-3-Clause       (extra: store)
  - fastapi             MIT License        (extra: server)
  - uvicorn             BSD-3-Clause       (extra: server)

Dependency-license note (not legal advice): OpenReagent deliberately avoids
linking, at import time, against any copyleft-licensed analysis framework so
that the Apache-2.0 license of this package is unencumbered. Where a more
capable but differently licensed tool would help, integrate it at arm's length
(as a separate process) rather than importing it into this package. See
docs/architecture.md for the rationale.
